What else have you got?

Use a tight story bank, not improvisation. Pick 6–8 stories from your own experience and map each to a few common themes: conflict, ambiguity, failure, leadership, impact, and learning. Then rehearse them out loud in a 60–90 second format: situation, what you did, result, and what you’d do differently. The freezing usually happens when you’re trying to invent the story and the structure at the same time.

For your profile, I’d anchor on stories from Guardio VIP support, Heseg team lead, and the Base44 MVP / AI bot work — those give you customer insight, cross-functional work, and initiative. If you want, I can run you through a mock first-round behavioral interview and push you when your answers get too vague.  
